message.content:
Below is a minimal example of an **interactive card** that rotates around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* Container that holds the card */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e 0%, #fad0c4 100%);
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform .6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;     /* Needed for 3D transforms */
  cursor: pointer;
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card::before,
.card::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide back side when rotated */
  border-radius: 12px;
}

/* Front content */
.card::before {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #fff;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 20px;
  background: inherit;
}

/* Back side of the card – rotated 180° so it shows on hover */
.card::after {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
  background: #fff;
  color: #333;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1rem;
  padding: 20px;
  text-align: center;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card"></div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Sets the 3D perspective for the card. |
| `.card` | The card container with a gradient background, rounded corners, shadow, and a smooth transition. |
| `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps child elements in 3D space. |
| `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside of each pseudo‑element when rotated. |
| `::before` | Represents the front side of the card (visible initially). |
| `::after` | Represents the back side of the card (rotated 180° so it becomes visible on hover). |

When you hover over the card, the `transform: rotateY(180deg)` property triggers a 3‑second rotation, revealing the back side. You can replace the gradient, text, or add images inside the pseudo‑elements to customize the card’s appearance.
